hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1484","Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj narrated to us, Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, and Salam bin Junada narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, narrated to us Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The most difficult prayer for the hypocrites is the last evening prayer.” And dawn, and if they knew what is in them, they would have come to them even if they were crawling. And I am most concerned that I command the prayer and it is performed, then I command a man to pray, then I take a bundle of Fire, so I will burn their houses for people who neglect to pray.” This is the hadith of Ibn Numayr, and in the hadith of Abu Muawiyah, he said: “I have become concerned,” and he said: Then I will order a man to lead the people in prayer, then I will go with me with men who have bundles of firewood to a people who do not witness the prayer, and I will burn their houses. \By fire\"""""""
"1485","It is narrated by Muhammad ibn al-Walid, it is narrated by Abd al-Wahhab, meaning al-Thaqafi, who said: I heard Yahya ibn Sa’id saying: I heard Nafi’ narrating that Abd Allah ibn Umar used to say: “When we missed a person in the last evening and morning prayers, we would have a bad suspicion of him.”"
